{"name":"Limón Fresco","hex":"#cebc55","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fresco","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cool, refreshing state of the air; coolness, duskiness, shade.","An artwork made by applying water-based pigment to wet or fresh lime mortar or plaster."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To paint using fresco."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fresco"}],"entries":[{"title":"Limón","blocks":[{"text":"Limón, also known as Puerto Limón, is the capital city of both the province and canton of the same name. One of Costa Rica's seven \"middle cities\", Limón has a population of 71,514, which made it, as of 2022, the most-populous city in the country outside of the Greater Metropolitan Area and the second most-populous district in the nation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Lim%C3%B3n_-_Panoramic_view_from_Downtown_Lim%C3%B3n.jpg/330px-Lim%C3%B3n_-_Panoramic_view_from_Downtown_Lim%C3%B3n.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lim%C3%B3n","wikidata":"Q30620"},{"title":"Fresco","blocks":[{"text":"Fresco is a technique of mural painting executed upon freshly laid (\"wet\") lime plaster. Water is used as the vehicle for the dry-powder pigment to merge with the plaster, and with the setting of the plaster, the painting becomes an integral part of the wall. The word fresco is derived from the Italian adjective fresco meaning \"fresh\", and may thus be contrasted with fresco-secco or secco mural painting techniques, which are applied to dried plaster, to supplement painting in fresco. The fresco technique has been employed since antiquity and is closely associated with Italian Renaissance painting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Creaci%C3%B3n_de_Ad%C3%A1n_%28Miguel_%C3%81ngel%29.jpg/330px-Creaci%C3%B3n_de_Ad%C3%A1n_%28Miguel_%C3%81ngel%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&